{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":503130,"name":"Bailey Johnson","username":"bjohnson1","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/b/53a042/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-28T22:56:38.039Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503130-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503130-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503130-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503130-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt appears that Grok Bot (in addition to Cursor cloud agents) may not respect the mcpServers optional field in the Cursor Plugin manifest ( \u003ca href=\"https://cursor.com/docs/reference/plugins#cursor-plugin-manifest\" class=\"inline-onebox\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ePlugins Reference | Cursor Docs\u003c/a\u003e ) used to override the default mcp.json discovery.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth Grok Bot and Cursor cloud agents failed to authenticate when a marketplace-listed plugin was added with a MCP config file named differently (even though it was provided in that optional manifest field).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThis does not appear to impact local Cursor agents.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRenaming the MCP config file to the standard “mcp.json” at the top level of the plugin repo + removing the mcpServers optional field from the manifest resolved the issue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503130-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503130-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd a marketplace listed plugin to Grok Bot/Cursor which provides the optional mcpServers field in the Cursor plugin manifest, with an MCP config file named something other than “mcp.json”.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAttempt to authenticate from Grok Bot or a Cursor cloud agent.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503130-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503130-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503130-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503130-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot v0.61.0\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor v3.22.12\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-503130-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-503130-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo - Cursor works, but with this issue\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":1,"updated_at":"2026-09-28T23:07:32.157Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":173273,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cursor-cloud-agents-not-respecting-mcpservers-optional-field","display_username":"Bailey Johnson","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"link_counts":[{"url":"https://cursor.com/docs/reference/plugins#cursor-plugin-manifest","internal":false,"reflection":false,"title":"Plugins Reference | Cursor Docs","clicks":0}],"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":140191,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"us